* =====================================================================================================
* ldo_3v3__rt9080.lib -- behavioural model of the Richtek RT9080 (fixed output, TSOT-23-5, no SNS pin)
*
* Part:       RT9080-33GJ5 (U1, main board, VSYS -> +3V3). The output option is a parameter (VNOM), so a
*             wrong variant in the BOM (e.g. RT9080-28GJ5) is simulated at its own output voltage.
* Datasheet:  Richtek DS9080-09, December 2024
*             https://www.richtek.com/assets/product_file/RT9080/DS9080-09.pdf
* No vendor SPICE model is published for the RT9080 (searched richtek.com and distributor listings, 2026-10),
* so this is a hand-built macro model. Each number cites the datasheet table or figure it comes from.
* "Fig." = Typical Operating Characteristics, DS section 16 (pages 8-11), read off the plots.
*
* MODELLED
*   Output voltage   VNOM*(1+ACC). ACC = accuracy corner, +/-2 % (Table 14, ILOAD = 1 mA, TA = 25 C).
*   Temp drift       Typical drift vs 25 C, Fig. "Output Voltage vs Temperature" (VOUT = 3.3 V, 1 mA):
*                    3.277 V @ -40 C, 3.301 @ -10, 3.320 @ 25, 3.328 @ 60, 3.329 @ 75. Fit (3.3 V option):
*                    dV = 0.42 mV/C*(T-25) - 4.8 uV/C^2*(T-25)^2, scaled by VNOM/3.32. Applied on top of ACC
*                    (the +/-2 % is a 25 C figure; the DS gives no over-temperature accuracy).
*   Line regulation  LINE = change over VNOM+1 .. 5.5 V as a fraction of VOUT: 0.13 % typ, 0.35 % max (Table 14).
*                    Sign is a corner. Extrapolated below VNOM+1 V, where Table 14 (VOUT+1 < VIN < 5.5 V) gives no
*                    guarantee. Low-passed at 16 Hz so that the DC term does not mask the AC PSRR below.
*   Load regulation  LREG = 0.5 % typ / 1 % max, 1-600 mA (Table 14): DC loop transconductance GDC = 0.6 A/(LREG*VNOM).
*   Dropout          PMOS RDS = 0.517 ohm typ (0.31 V / 0.6 A), 0.883 ohm max (0.53 V / 0.6 A): Table 14 "Dropout
*                    Voltage, 3 V <= VOUT", 25 C. RDSK = 1 (typ) or 1.71 (max). Temperature +0.28 %/C from Fig.
*                    "Dropout Voltage vs Temperature" (3.3 V, 600 mA: 250 mV @ -40 C, 305 @ 25, 390 @ 125). Gate drive:
*                    RDS ~ 2.7 V/(VIN - 0.9 V), fitted to the Table 14 rows of the lower options (VIN = VOUT+VDROP:
*                    1.33 ohm @ 1.93 V, 1.18 @ 2.06, 0.95 @ 2.2-2.5, 0.68 @ 2.7, 0.60 @ 3.1, 0.517 @ 3.6).
*   Current limit    ILIM 1.1 A typ / 610 mA min, no max (Table 14, VOUT = 90 %); Fig. "Current Limit vs Temperature"
*                    gives ~0.98 A for the 3.3 V option (default). Fold-back to IFB ~0.72 A at VOUT = 0 (Fig.
*                    "Fold-Back Current Limit vs Temperature", 3.3 V; section 18.3 "around 0.6 A"), linear up to
*                    VOUT = 90 % of VNOM.
*   Enable/UVLO      EN rising threshold 0.67 V (Fig. "Enable Threshold vs Input Voltage", VIN >= 2 V; Table 14
*                    VEN_R <= 0.9 V). Operating input >= 1.2 V (Recommended Operating Conditions); the model is off
*                    below VINMIN = 1.2 V, where behaviour is not specified.
*   Soft start       Exponential reference ramp, TSS = 70 us, from Fig. "Power On from EN" (VIN 4 V, VOUT 3.3 V:
*                    67 % at ~65 us, 92 % at ~195 us, 98 % at ~390 us). Typical only; no min/max in the DS.
*   Quiescent        IQ 2 uA typ / 4 uA max at no load (Table 14); input current at no load = IQ exactly.
*                    Load-dependent GND current IG(I) = 0.3m*I^0.25*(1-exp(-I/0.3 mA)) + 0.82m*I (A, I in A), a
*                    smooth fit of Fig. "Ground Current vs Load Current" (VIN 4.3 V, VOUT 3.3 V, 25 C: 57 uA @ 1 mA,
*                    105 @ 10 mA, 205 @ 50 mA, 270 @ 100 mA, 760 @ 600 mA; fit within -13..+3 %). Below 1 mA the DS
*                    has no data: IG fades ~linearly to 0 (ASSUMPTION; bench-verify the sleep current).
*   Feedback divider Internal VOUT -> GND load IDIV = 0.5 uA, counted inside IQ (value not published, ASSUMPTION).
*   Discharge        80 ohm output pull-down when disabled (Table 14 RDISCHG, section 17.7).
*   Body diode       VOUT -> VIN (abs max VOUT - VIN <= 0.3 V, section 10). No reverse channel current.
*   Loop dynamics    Output-voltage referred two-path error amplifier: fast proportional path GHF = beta*GHF1 and slow
*                    high-gain path GLF = GDC - GHF (first-order lag TAU1), summed, then one pole FA; beta = 0.8 V/VNOM
*                    (0.8 V reference + internal divider, block diagram section 9). Fitted to Fig. "Load Transient"
*                    (RT9080-08, 1 mA -> 600 mA in ~20 us, COUT 1 uF): DS ~27 mV undershoot, ~23 mV overshoot, ~4 mV
*                    settled; model 66 / 24 / 3.8 mV with GHF1 = 5 S, TAU1 = 70 us, FA = 600 kHz (undershoot 2.5x
*                    pessimistic). Checked by test_ldo_3v3.py::test_model_matches_datasheet_figures. The loop speed is
*                    fixed; the real part has adaptive bias and is slower at uA loads, which the DS does not
*                    characterise. SLOW multiplies both time constants for sensitivity runs.
*   Anti-windup      Back-calculation: the slow path may ask for at most what the pass device can deliver in its
*                    present state (min of current limit and dropout current) + 5 mA, as a saturating amplifier does in
*                    dropout or current limit. Dropout recovery is not characterised in the DS (ASSUMPTION).
*   PSRR             GRO = 8.4 mS (VIN -> VOUT conductance) gives 76 dB at 1 kHz (Table 14: 75 dB at VIN 3 V, VOUT 2.5 V,
*                    50 mA, 1 uF), 65 dB at 10 kHz and 37 dB at 100 kHz (Fig. "PSRR vs Frequency", 2.8 V / 50 mA / 1 uF:
*                    ~62 and ~40 dB). GFF = 30 mS with TFF = 1 us (gate-coupling high-pass) gives +4.6 / -1.8 mV on
*                    Fig. "Line Transient" (VIN 2.8 -> 3.8 V, VOUT 1.8 V, 1 mA: about +4.6 / -3 mV). GRO and GFF scale
*                    with the pass current (as gds and gm do) through a 1 us-lagged copy of IG, normalised to 600 mA.
*
* NOT MODELLED
*   Over-temperature shutdown (150 C typ, 20 C hysteresis): the test computes TJ from theta-JA(EVB) = 100.7 C/W
*   (DS section 13) instead. Output noise. PSRR peaking near 0.5-1 MHz (Fig.: ~25-30 dB; model ~37 dB, optimistic).
*   IQ / GND current vs temperature and vs VIN (only 25 C, VIN 4.3 V curves exist) and in dropout. The real internal
*   compensation (unpublished): dynamics are only fitted at the DS conditions. Adaptive-bias slow-down at light
*   load (use SLOW). Spread of soft start, EN threshold, fold-back current and the maximum current limit.
*
* Pins: VIN EN VOUT GND
* =====================================================================================================
.subckt LDO3V3_RT9080 VIN EN VOUT GND params: VNOM=3.3 ACC=0 TEMPC=25 RDSK=1 LREG=0.005 LINE=0.0013
+ ILIM=0.98 IFB=0.72 IQ=2u TSS=70u RDIS=80 VENTH=0.67 VINMIN=1.2 GHF1=5 TAU1=70u FA=600k GRO=8.4m
+ GFF=30m TFF=1u SLOW=1 IDIV=0.5u
.param BETA={0.8/VNOM}
.param GDC={0.6/(LREG*VNOM)}
.param GHF={BETA*GHF1}
.param GLF={max(GDC-GHF, 0.01)}
.param XL={1.5*ILIM/GLF}
.param DVT={(0.42e-3*(TEMPC-25) - 4.8e-6*(TEMPC-25)*(TEMPC-25))/3.32}
.param RDS0={0.517*RDSK*(1+0.0028*(TEMPC-25))}
.param TAUA={1/(6.283185*FA)}
* IG at the divider current, removed from the GND pin so that the no-load input current equals IQ
.param IG0={3.0e-4*pwr(IDIV*IDIV+1e-14, 0.125)*(1-exp(-IDIV/0.3m)) + 8.2e-4*IDIV}
* enable (EN threshold and minimum operating input), 0..1
Bena ena 0 V = 0.25*(1+tanh((V(EN,GND)-VENTH)/0.02))*(1+tanh((V(VIN,GND)-VINMIN)/0.02))
Rena ena 0 1G
* set point: accuracy corner, temperature drift, line regulation (low-passed, extrapolated outside VNOM+1..5.5 V)
Bln lnt 0 V = LINE*(V(VIN,GND)-(VNOM+1))/(5.5-(VNOM+1))
Rln lnt lnr 10Meg
Cln lnr 0 1n
Bset set 0 V = VNOM*(1+ACC)*(1+DVT)*(1 + V(lnr))*V(ena)
* soft start: exponential reference ramp, tau = TSS
Rss set ss {TSS/1n}
Css ss 0 1n
* error (output referred)
Berr err 0 V = V(ss) - V(VOUT,GND)
Rerr err 0 1G
* pass-current-dependent bias = (IQ + IG(I)) / IG(600 mA); lags 1 us (breaks the algebraic ip -> bias -> ip loop).
* Used only to scale GRO and GFF.
Gbias 0 bias cur = ((IQ + (3.0e-4*pow(V(ip)*V(ip)+1e-14, 0.125)*(1-exp(-abs(V(ip))/0.3m)) + 8.2e-4*abs(V(ip))))/758u - V(bias))*1n/1u
Cbias bias 0 1n
Rbias bias 0 1T
* slow high-gain path: first-order lag TAU1 with back-calculation anti-windup (target <= (iav + 5 mA)/GLF)
Gx1 0 x1 cur = (max(min(min(V(err), (V(iav) + 5m)/GLF), XL), -XL) - V(x1))*1n/TAU1/SLOW
Cx1 x1 0 1n
Rx1 x1 0 1T
* control current (A, as a voltage) with the amplifier pole FA; target clamped to -0.2 A .. 1.5*ILIM
Gctl 0 ctl cur = (max(min(GHF*V(err) + GLF*V(x1), 1.5*ILIM), -0.2) - V(ctl))*1n/TAUA/SLOW
Cctl ctl 0 1n
Rctl ctl 0 1T
* pass device limits: triode (dropout) resistance vs gate drive, current limit with fold-back
Brds rds 0 V = RDS0*2.7/max(V(VIN,GND)-0.9, 0.3)
Rrds rds 0 1G
Blim lim 0 V = IFB + (ILIM-IFB)*max(min(V(VOUT,GND)/(0.9*VNOM), 1), 0)
Rlim lim 0 1G
Btri tri 0 V = (V(VIN,GND)-V(VOUT,GND))/V(rds)
Rtri tri 0 1G
* demand = control current + PMOS output conductance (DC PSRR) + gate-coupling high-pass (HF line feedthrough);
* the loop trims ctl to cancel the last two at low frequency. GRO/GFF are calibrated at 50 mA (bias 0.268).
Rlp VIN vlp {TFF/1n}
Clp vlp GND 1n
Bdem dem 0 V = V(ctl) + V(bias)/0.268*(GRO*(V(VIN,GND)-V(VOUT,GND)) + GFF*(V(VIN,GND)-V(vlp,GND)))
Rdem dem 0 1G
* available current (anti-windup reference) and the pass current: smooth minimum of demand, limit and dropout
Biav iav 0 V = 0.5*(V(lim)+V(tri) - sqrt((V(lim)-V(tri))*(V(lim)-V(tri)) + 1e-6))
Riav iav 0 1G
Bm1 m1 0 V = 0.5*(V(dem)+V(lim) - sqrt((V(dem)-V(lim))*(V(dem)-V(lim)) + 1e-6))
Rm1 m1 0 1G
Bmn mn 0 V = 0.5*(V(m1)+V(tri) - sqrt((V(m1)-V(tri))*(V(m1)-V(tri)) + 1e-6))
Rmn mn 0 1G
* no reverse channel current: soft clamp at 0 (softplus, 1 uA knee)
Bip ip 0 V = V(ena)*0.5*(V(mn) + sqrt(V(mn)*V(mn) + 1e-12))
Rip ip 0 1G
Bpass VIN VOUT I = V(ip)
* ground-pin current: IQ (less the divider share) plus IG(I); shutdown 0.1 uA (Table 14 ISHDN)
Bgnd VIN GND I = V(ena)*(IQ - IDIV - IG0 + (3.0e-4*pow(V(ip)*V(ip)+1e-14, 0.125)*(1-exp(-abs(V(ip))/0.3m)) + 8.2e-4*abs(V(ip)))) + (1-V(ena))*0.1u
* internal feedback divider (inside the DS IQ)
Bdiv VOUT GND I = IDIV*V(VOUT,GND)/VNOM
* active discharge when disabled (80 ohm)
Bdis VOUT GND I = (1-V(ena))*V(VOUT,GND)/RDIS
* PMOS body diode
Dbody VOUT VIN LDO3V3_DBODY
.model LDO3V3_DBODY D(IS=1e-12 N=1.2 RS=0.2)
.ends LDO3V3_RT9080
